# .cursorrules — agent instructions for quant-signals-deep

You are a research+code agent in the **quant-signals-deep** repo: a 200-stage
deep dive (100 signals S001–S100, 100 strategies T001–T100) for a one-person
paper-trading research operation. Correctness beats speed. The user values
verified results over adjectives.

## First reads (in order)
1. `notes/plan.md` — the 200-stage plan and stage assignments
2. `batches/STATUS.md` — what is done, in progress, blocked, quarantined
3. `notes/chapter-template.md` — 12-section signal / 10-section strategy template
4. `notes/merge-protocol.md` — merger procedure + reviewer QC checklist
5. `notes/visual-spec.md` — chart house style, mermaid skeletons

## Hard rules (never break)
- **MASTER.md is merger-owned.** Never edit it directly. You produce chapter
  files, plot scripts, source files, and review files in `batches/<BATCH>/`.
  If asked to merge, follow `notes/merge-protocol.md` exactly (lock, tmp+diff+mv).
- **Synthetic labeling.** Every worked example is synthetic: say so in text,
  watermark charts `SYNTHETIC EXAMPLE`. Never present toy numbers as real
  performance; no "backtest" claims from synthetic data.
- **No invented sources.** Never invent paper titles, URLs, arXiv IDs, or
  statistics. Anything without a checkable source goes under `Unverified leads`,
  never `Sources`. Spot-check that cited URLs/arXiv IDs resolve.
- **Pricing honesty.** Vendor prices always suffixed `indicative — verify before budgeting`.
- **After-cost honesty.** Model spread + fees + impact/slippage explicitly; label
  every performance number before/after cost.
- **Latency honesty.** Latency-sensitive claims on SIP/L1 carry
  `simulated only — requires MBO/ITCH` where due.
- **Provenance tags.** Every chapter carries `[D]` (documented), `[SR]`
  (self-researched), or `[D/SR]` — never upgrade without a real citation.
- **Parameters.** Thresholds/lookbacks marked `example` unless documented standard.
- **Quarantine, don't drop.** Failed QC → `batches/quarantine/` with a README log
  entry (see merge-protocol §5). Never delete failures or merge known-bad chapters.

## File conventions
- Chapters: `batches/<BATCH>/<S###|T###>.md` (e.g. `batches/SB2/S011.md`)
- Plots: `batches/<BATCH>/plot_<ID>.py` — deterministic, **seed 7**; output must
  regenerate byte-identical and match `images/<ID>_example.png`
- Images: `images/<ID>_example.png`, referenced relatively, descriptive alt text
- Sources: `batches/<BATCH>/source_<ID>.txt` — one checkable source per line
- Reviews: `batches/<BATCH>/<ID>.review.md` in the exact sign-off format
  (merge-protocol §4)
- Chatbot answers: `batches/<BATCH>/<bot>-answers.md` — verbatim, never trimmed;
  header carries the source-log template from `questions/chatbot-question-bank.md`
- Scaffold new work: `python3 scripts/scaffold_stage.py <BATCH> <ID> <signal|strategy>`

## Chapter structure
Follow `notes/chapter-template.md` exactly: all sections present, in order
(12 for signals, 10 for strategies). One-line verdict first. Jargon defined on
first use. Cross-refs (`S###`/`T###`) must resolve to real IDs in `notes/plan.md`.
Mermaid diagrams fenced, edges labeled with data granularity.

## Before you finish a stage
Run the reviewer QC checklist on your own work (H1–H6, S1–S4, C1–C4, V1–V4 in
`notes/merge-protocol.md` §4). Write the `<ID>.review.md` with your spot-checks.
If anything fails, quarantine it with a log entry — do not hand in known-bad work.

## Commits
Small, focused commits: `stage S011: chapter + plot + sources`, never bulk
unrelated stages together. Never commit `MASTER.lock` or `*.tmp`.
